Carafe bench: vertex shader inputs past GL_MAX_VERTEX_ATTRIBS read as (0, 0, 0, 1) in OpenGL.
Mesa's d3d12 driver has 16 vertex attributes, and DXVK's fixed-function vertex shader declares generic
inputs 16 and 17. The GLSL program failed to link ("invalid explicit location 16"), so NFSU's full-screen
colour pass drew with no vertex shader and painted the frame black. Eden never enables those attributes in
OpenGL, so the first stage now treats them as not written: they are not declared and read as the defaults.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

